This modification will detect when:
1. The tag is negative (less than JS_TAG_FIRST)
2. But isn't actually one of the valid string tags (JS_TAG_STRING or JS_TAG_STRING_ROPE)

The bug could manifest when invalid tag values are passed to the function, causing it to potentially return incorrect results for negative tags that aren't actually string tags. The added check will log these cases while maintaining the original behavior.
